WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.060
Nought point nine nine.

2
00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:04.600
Nought point nine nine nine.

3
00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:07.700
Each extra nine creeps closer to one.

4
00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:10.250
Now keep writing nines, forever.

5
00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:12.430
There is never a last digit.

6
00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:15.310
Is that never-ending number exactly one?

7
00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.870
Or does it always fall
just a tiny bit short?

8
00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:23.170
In this mission, you'll turn fractions
into decimals by dividing the numerator

9
00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:24.730
by the denominator.

10
00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:27.650
You'll see that some
fractions stop, but others,

11
00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:31.360
like one third, give
decimals that repeat forever.

12
00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:35.230
And you'll find out what those
repeating decimals really are.

13
00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:40.520
Your mission: decide whether nought point
nine recurring is exactly equal to one.
